Subject: Cantor Procedure Tool CLI Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 242353de-dded-4146-93bd-94c3777cf7dd
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_CLI.sop

& [Need] is demonstrated
  + the semantic query CLI and MCP already work but do not serialize the process-procedure fake controller
  + CPPE-I08 is callable only as a Rust library or test, limiting controller interoperability experiments
  + a stable subprocess boundary is the smallest realistic demonstration that no llama.cpp modification is required

& [ChosenSolution] is minimal
  + add one binary to the existing cantor_cli package
  + reuse public cantor_core types and functions without duplicating semantic logic
  + expose schema, run, and verify so generation and independent checking remain separable

& [Alternatives] were rejected
  + adding cantor.exchange to the signed SOP MCP server would conflate two authorities and require a different runtime dependency
  + modifying llama.cpp before proving the ordinary tool boundary would add provider-specific risk without evidence
  + a resident service would add persistence and lifecycle complexity not required for the experiment
  + placing transport code in cantor_core would mix process I/O with the effectless semantic core

& [Value] is concrete
  + any local controller capable of JSON subprocess calls can inspect the schema, run the fake checkpoint, and verify an outcome
  + exact response and exit behavior becomes testable across language and provider boundaries
  + later work gains evidence about the external seam while every neural and provider claim remains residualized
